<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Can vei la lauzeta mover</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Can vei la lauzeta mover&quot; is a song in the Occitan language by Bernart de Ventadorn, a troubadour of the 12th century. It is among the oldest and the best known of all troubadour songs. Both its words and its melody survive, in variants from three different <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. Its lauzeta is a lark. The song is a first-person poem of seven stanzas of eight lines each, with a closing coda of four lines.</p></div>
